  "description": "The build-time library a build program calls to build the Rust WebAssembly frontend of a CodeBrix.WebPlatform application: it checks the prerequisites and says what is missing, writes the client code generated from the compiled backend, the platform's shared Rust crate, the platform's Rust crates (carried as one archive, with their notices) and the cargo configuration into the frontend, so that plain cargo works there offline, and runs the Dioxus build tool to build or serve the site, shrinking release builds with the packaged wasm-opt. No Node.js. It is used while an application is built and is not part of the built application.",
